\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Seen Stabilizing \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 1998\par 09:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Monday, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to stabilize around its current levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0635 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,295 and ROL9,315, up from ROL9,280 and ROL9,300 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu is expected to steady around ROL9,300 per dollar, with little pressure from importers' dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The pressure on the leu decreased late last week as banks and exporters sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  The move followed a stormy beginning of the week when the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and selling dollars to halt the leu's falls. Dealers said the bank sold around $30 million when the dollar rose to about ROL9,400. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted the leu will continue to depreciate by 3% per month against the dollar by the end of the year, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintaining tight control and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop any major moves. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate remained Monday at 70%, unchanged from Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again seen attracting leu deposits at high rates Friday in order to divert funds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-10