\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Ctrl Bank Action Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 1998\par 09:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Monday, with dealers saying the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  At 0640 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,320 and ROL9,340, from ROL9,300 and ROL9,320 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu depreciated on both speculative trading by banks and increasing dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and selling dollars Friday to calm the leu depreciation and dealers predicted the move may be repeated Monday. \par \par \uc2  But they said the trend would continue as banks are interested in buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the leu depreciation is needed in order to control the trade deficit that has widened in the first seven months of the year to $1.66 billion from $1.36 billion in the corresponding period in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate rose Monday to 50%, from 40% early Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0736GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916dua508hah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
