\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  leu ends weaker despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 1998\par 16:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1330 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended lower on Friday at 9,300/20 to the dollar from Thursday's 9,275/95 on banks' large hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases and despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (BNR) medium-sized dollar sales to ease pressure on the leu. \par \par \uc2  *"Many banks continued to extend their long dollar positions seeing the greenback as a better investment than placements on the money market, where short-term rates are still lower and less attractive than in mid-September," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In mid-September short-term rates exceeded 100 percent due to banks building up minimum reserves. \par \par \uc2  "Position adjustment combined with an increased demand for dollars from seasonal importers and expectations of further depreciation put higher pressure on the leu," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BNR had sold dollars for about 9,270 lei to temper demand shortly before closing giving the leu some relief. But the unit fell back as demand remained relatively high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Further BNR moves to prevent the leu from sliding are likely to occur next week, one trader said. \par \par \uc2  * Money-market short-term prices closed at around 50/60 percent, almost flat on Thursday's levels, in a fairly liquid money market. \par \par \uc2  Operators expected no large swings early next week, saying prices were likely to remain relatively stable. \par \par \uc2  "As long as money market rates are at the present level, many players will continue to buy dollars, triggering fresh pressure on the leu," another trader said. "Nobody will risk going short on hard curency to speculate on the money market." \par \par \uc2  * Leu-dollar prices at licensed exchange houses weakened to about 9,290/9,500 from around 9,120/300 on Thursday. ((Andrei Iva, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua20176g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
