\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Calm Session Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1998\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Monday, with dealers predicting no major change over the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0630 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,105 and ROL9,120, from ROL9,090 and ROL9,110 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu is expected to stabilize around the current rate and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation over the past week had been caused more by speculative trading by banks rather than dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the pressure on the leu was low, with no major dollar demand from importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer predicted the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any major depreciation of the leu. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate rose to around 140% Monday, from 125% Friday, as banks tried to attract leu deposits to meet the minimum reserve requirements set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu Saturday predicted a stabile money market and inflation on track by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  But he said the government must speed up privatization and structural reform of state-owned enterprises or face "a more drastic reduction of budget expenditure or devastating inflation." \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0658