\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early On Speculative Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 1998\par 09:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Friday on speculative moves from banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0645 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,095 and ROL9,115, from ROL9,070 and ROL9,090 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu has depreciated more on speculative trading from banks rather than dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  He said that banks have sold and bought dollars "on spot" with the payment in two days to take advantage of the high money market rates. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate rose at around 125% Friday, from 110% Thursday, as banks try to attract leu deposits to meet the minimum reserve requirements set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a further depreciation but said the exchange rate should stay around ROL9,100 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in the last week, selling dollars to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade at more than ROL9,100. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu said the leu would depreciate between 1.5% and 2% monthly by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-09-