\par\par \b \uc2  Romania c.bank sells dollar to cap leu slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1998\par 13:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Sept 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, selling moderate amounts of dollars on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent a depreciation of the leu, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR sold relatively modest amounts of dollars to cap the leu's slide," said one dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the unit came under pressure in early trading when it touched levels of about 9,060/9,080 to the dollar. They said increased dollar demand followed larger buy notes from importers. \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed for a short time at rates of about 9,020/9,035 to the dollar after the BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but eventually it bounced back to around 9,035/9,050 to the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the BNR also drained leu funds, pushing up one-week rates at 75/95 percent from 70/85 percent from opening levels to ease the pressure on the leu. ((Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9900qb3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
