\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Against Dollar In Early Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1998\par 09:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--Romania's leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Tuesday, with dealers predicting the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  At 0650 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL8,920 and ROL8,940, up from between ROL8,915 and ROL8,930 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will stay almost unchanged over the session, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signaled that a further depreciation isn't welcome. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars at the end of last week, as the dollar was trading for more than ROL9,000. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the depreciation in the past week's stormy sessions was needed, as the leu was "too strong" and the exchange rate hurt exports, unbalancing the trade deficit. \par \par \uc2  Calm was restored in the money market, meanwhile, as banks have completed their end-of-month minimum reserve requirements, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate is at 45%, from about 80% Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0737GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9107g3i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
