\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Dn Vs Dlr Early;Further Depreciation Predicted \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 09:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Friday, with dealers predicting the depreciation might continue. \par \par \uc2  At 0710 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL8,795 and ROL8,815, up from between ROL8,780 and ROL8,800 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "From now on, we might see a more substantial depreciation," said a dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest. \par \par \uc2  He predicted the dollar might be traded at more than ROL8,850 by the end of the session if \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's National Bank doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to calm down the depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The leu began depreciating Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at ROL8,745, signaling it would allow a depreciating trend. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the depreciation was needed as an overvalued leu hurts Romania's trade deficit. \par \par \uc2  According to official statistics, Romania's trade deficit in the first five months of the year was $1.15 billion, up from $818.6 million in the corresponding period in 1997. \par \par \uc2  Exports in May amounted to $661.2 million, from $648.3 million in April and down 9.9% from May 1997 \par \par \uc2  Imports in May amounted to $1.03 billion, up 6.6% from April, and up 3.1% compared with May 1997. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates rose to 50% Friday, from 45% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2