\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Steady Vs Dlr Early; Shrugs Off Russian Crisis \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 09:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Friday, showing little reaction to the crisis on Russian financial markets, with dealers predicting calm trading over the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0700 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL8,725 and ROL8,745, hardly changed from Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu was little affected by turmoil on Russian markets. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt we will see any effect, our market is too closed," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The leu fell slightly against the dollar on Thursday after posting gains throughout the week. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said that dollar buying Thursday had been triggered by low money market rates, which had led banks to show interest in buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate remained at 20% Friday, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the slight decline is also a result of increasing dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  He predicted the leu is likely to fall further in the coming week but said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which monitors the market closely, is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop any major fluctuations. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Mugur Isarescu said earlier this summer that he expects the leu to depreciate by the end of the year but declined to give a precise estimate. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98 \par \par