\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Steady Vs Dollar In Early Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 09:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Monday, with dealers predicting no major change over the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0655 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL8,740 and ROL8,760, roughly the same as Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest predicted the unit will stay at the same level with the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop any major change. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars on Friday as the leu appreciated, with the dollar trading between ROL8,715 and ROL8,725. \par \par \uc2  "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) signaled it wanted to buy any dollar surplus on the market," the dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu suggested last week he wants to start boosting the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  He said the bank will buy more dollars to meet its 1998 target of $3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the end of June totaled $2.43 billion, down from $2.52 billion a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate went up to 25% Monday from 10% Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted increased stability on the money market as a result of the new rules imposed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on banks Aug. 1. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretza