\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1998\par 14:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, July 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and sold what local dealers said were significant amounts of dollars to prevent the local leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from further depreciating. \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed to around 8,680/690 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from previous levels of some 8,705/715. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BNR also took one-week leu deposits to drain a part of the excess leu funds. One-week prices remained almost unchanged after the BNR move, with rates hovering around 25/45 percent. \par \par \uc2  The money market has been liquid in the past few weeks, with high liquidity also confirmed by the over-subscription of a 91-day T-bill issue sold on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The T-bill average annual yield eased to 42.92 percent from 43.86 percent last week. ((Andrei Iva, Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7801fse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
