\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2 's leu ends weaker on cen bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1355 GMT - The Romanian leu closed around 8,560/95 to the dollar on Monday, weaker than Friday's close of 8,540/60 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar supply increased in early mornig, but thin hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand triggered firmer leu-dollar rates of 8,535/50," one dealer said. The BNR stepped into the market at that point and depressed prices to around 8,550 to the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  * Dealers said the higher dollar sales originated with banks needing leu funds for corporate clients and to complete their minimum required reserves at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  * Market operators expected the market to trade similarily over the next few days. They said the BNR would closely monitor the market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the leu firmed. \par \par \uc2  * On the money market, short-term prices rose to 90 percent for one-week leu funds from some 80 percent in early trading. Traders said prices might climb further by the end of the week as several banks needed leu funds for their reserves. \par \par \uc2  * Leu-dollar retail prices were unchanged at about 8,560/650. ((Andrei Iva, Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02dtm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
