\par\par \b \uc2  Romania c.bank buys dollars-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, June 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market on Thursday to temper the appreciation of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR bought small amounts of dollars to prevent the leu from firming sharply after the unit had appreciated to 8,460/480 in early trading," one said. \par \par \uc2  The leu opened at around 8,495/525 to the dollar on Thursday, a shade weaker than the previous day's close of 8,490/520. \par \par \uc2  It firmed afterwards as dollar supply rose. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it was difficult to plot a trend for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the rest of the day. "It all depends on the BNR and we don't know what its plans are," said one. \par \par \uc2  Short-term rates on the money market opened at around 65 percent and operators expected them to move up if the leu continued to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  Retail prices for the leu bobbed around 8,580/650 to the dollar. ((Andrei Iva, Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02rg6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
