\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to temper leu fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, March 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold dollars on the interbank market at midday after the leu weakened to about 8,500/600 to the dollar due to larger hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BNR sold some $4 million so far," said one trader, adding that its prices were near 8,400. \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed toward opening quotes of 8,350/400 to the dollar after the BNR moves, but remained weaker than last Friday's close of 8,250/350. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said higher dollar demand came from some repatriation of fixed income investments and on the back of a cash-heavy money market. \par \par \uc2  The leu's slide follows weeks of stability at prices near 8,055 to the dollar amid low hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand and attractive money market prices, which stood at 90/100 percent until late last week. \par \par \uc2  Some players said the BNR was also draining some leu funds from the money market, where rates hovered now at 65/75 percent. ((Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3n08y7w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
