\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Weakens Early As Oil Importers Seek Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 09:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--Romania's leu was weakening slightly in early trading Friday as oil importers started buying dollars to pay off maturing letters of credit in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading between 8,115 lei (ROL) and ROL8,160 at 0735 GMT Friday, from between ROL8,100 and ROL8,140 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said state oil importers will likely continue buying $1 million or so per day until the middle of next week to pay off maturing debts. \par \par \uc2  However, he indicated the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the leu starts to depreciate by more than ROL40 against dollar in a single day. \par \par \uc2  Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  'thinks that any fast depreciation could start a lot of speculation and turn into a run,' said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely borrow lei from the market Friday to reduce high liquidity. \par \par \uc2  He said liquidity, traditionally high in the first week of the month, was increased further by the lack of a Treasury bill auction this week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer said the Finance Ministry scheduled an auction of about\par ROL250 billion lei in three-month T-bills for next Tuesday.\par     -By Adam Brown; 401-210-8197 adam@mail.kappa.ro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0803GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument d