\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Weakens Early As Oil Importers Seen Seeking Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 08:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--Romania's leu is weakening slightly in early trading Thursday and dealers predicted increased dollar demand from oil importers in coming days. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading between 8,100 lei (ROL) and ROL8,140 at 0715 GMT Thursday, from between ROL8,090 and ROL8,115 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said state oil importers will have to buy several million dollars in the coming days to pay off maturing letters of credit in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the increased dollar demand and current high leu liquidity could weaken the leu by the outset of next week. \par \par \uc2  But another dealer predicted the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any depreciation despite analysts' claims that the leu is steeply overvalued. \par \par \uc2  After much fluctuation throughout the second half of 1997, the leu is trading at around levels from one year ago. Meanwhile, inflation in the last twelve months has totaled approximately 140%. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears that any depreciation could spark a round of speculation amid a continuing political crisis. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As reported, many government-allied and opposition politicians demand\par the resignation of Prime Minister Victor Ciorbea before the 1998 budget\par is presented to parliament next week.\par     -By Adam Brown (401)210-8197 adam@mail.kappa.ro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-03-98\par \f28 \par \par