\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA \highlight\uc2  CEN.BANK  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES \highlight\uc2  TO PROP UP EXPOSED LEU. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mirela Eremia \par \uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Jan 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on money and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday to ease pressure on the leu amid rising dollar demand and an end to limits on individuals' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases. \par \par \uc2  The leu dipped about two percent on the interbank market, closing at 8,330/400 to the dollar, while retail prices remained relatively stable at 8,350/500. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded briefly after the BNR drained money market funds and sold modest amounts of dollars. \par \par \uc2  Most traders said the BNR's moves had failed to dissipate expectations of higher pressure on the unit. Leu liquidity is seen up and, while exchange offices were free of crowds, Romanians were still digesting the new regulations. \par \par \uc2  "Next week will be interesting," said one trader. "Much depends on what the BNR does. But higher bank deposit rates and maybe fresh government bonds issues for individuals could help offset the psychological impact of the rules." \par \par \uc2  Romania introduced new rules aligned to the International Monetary Fund's article eight on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  convertibility. These lifted the $500 annual limit on Romanians' hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases and allowed access to the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  The move had been carefully prepared for months by the BNR, which has pledged to take whatever action is needed to keep the leu from sliding too quickly. \par \par \uc2  With the new rules, Romania agrees not to impose curbs on payments and transfers for current account deals, essentially foreign trade, and not to operate multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes. \par \par \uc2  But it can restrict capital movements. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials have repeateadly said the bank is prepared to keep a tight grip on the market. \par \par \uc2  Weeks of political turmoil, culminating in the walkout from the coalition cabinet on Thursday of its second largest party, the Social Democrats, have had little effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the party pledged to support the coalition in parliament. \par \par \uc2  Traders said no pressure had been detected from retail investors so far. Friday's slide, they said, could have been triggered by banks shifting to long dollar positions after staying short at the end of the month to meet minimum reserves. \par \par \uc2  Other operators said Romanians were likely to stick to a wait-and-see attitude as most banks increased deposit rates in response to rapid sales of high-interest government bonds. \par \par \uc2  "The bond sale was a clever move," said one dealer. "People were attracted by the new opportunities and if the Finance Ministry puts such papers on sale again the leu will gain." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Daniel Daianu said on Thursday before his departure for the World Economic Forum in Davos that he was confident the BNR "has full control of the situation. I'm not afraid of what might happen in the period ahead." \par \par \uc2  But he added that the leu's trend would depend on how solid an economic programme was put together by the revamped cabinet to emerge from this week's political upheaval. \par \par \uc2  Exchange house managers said no significant changes of their market features were likely ahead of the weekend. But some were reluctant to predict trends for next week. \par \par \uc2  "It's too soon to say what will happen. But in view of the BNR's efforts to create leu shortages it's possible there will be no spectacular shifts," said IDM exchange manager Dan Simionescu. \par \par \uc2  ((Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)) REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du1u00sa1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
