\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Leu Closes Stable With No Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1998\par 14:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu closed steady Friday with very little \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the ongoing political crisis, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at between 8,420 lei (ROL) and ROL8,460 Friday, about the same as opening. \par \par \uc2  'I didn't see any big dollar demand,' said one dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest. 'My clients have T-bills maturing and I know they're going to roll them over. There hasn't been any repatriation.' The dealer said many clients believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain the leu basically steady until the end of the current political crisis. \par \par \uc2  'The crisis will be over in three months, no matter how they resolve it,' predicted the dealer. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 16-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1326GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1g00ej6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
