\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Leu Stable As Dealers Await T-Bills,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par 09:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu is trading stable early Tuesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers predicted some strengthening in the afternoon on a large Treasury bill auction and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading between 8,450 and 8,570 lei at 0730 GMT, about the same as closing Monday. \par \par \uc2  One dealer with a foreign bank said the National Bank of Romania sale of $30 million Monday has halted the leu's slide, but said dollar demand and leu liquidity remain high. He predicted either further dollar sales or liquidity drain Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowed about 120 billion lei from the interbank market Monday at overnight rates of about 90%, but said leu liquidity is high Tuesday and predicted a slight drop in the money market rates despite the T-bill auction. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the government will offer 999 billion lei in the Tuesday T-bill auction, up from the originally scheduled offer of 642 billion lei. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer predicted T-bill yields as low as 75% on Tuesday's auction,\par from 90% last week and 120% in a late December auction.\par -By Adam Brown (401)210-8197 adam@mail.kappa.ro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0803GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1d00asu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\