\par\par \b \uc2  C.BANK  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES \highlight\uc2  ON THE MARKET-DEALERS. \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Jan 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold dollars on the local interbank market and soaked up money market funds in a repeated move in recent days to ease pressure on the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR sold dollars near 8,220/8,230. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The amounts were not significant. I can't see the reason why it did it as the market was relatively quiet today," another said. \par \par \uc2  The leu traded at around 8,235/280 to the dollar at mid-day after weakening to about 8,250/300 in early trading. Traders said the BNR mopped up overnight funds at prices near 90 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said the BNR moves were intended to keep money market liquidity tight and prevent pressures on the leu. ((Bucharest newsroom +40 1 312 0264, fax +40 1 315 8448)) REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du1700q56\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
