\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Weakens Slightly On Increased Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par 09:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (AP-Dow Jones)--Romania's leu is weakening slightly early Thursday on increased dollar buying, mostly from importers, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading between 7,985 and 8,015 lei on the interbank market at 10:00 local time (0800 GMT), from between 7,980 and 8,010 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  One dealer with a foreign bank said importers were likely buying more dollars than usual Wednesday as lei liquidity remains high on the market. He also said some foreign portfolio investors are repatriating some profits from local stock markets before the year end. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on money markets Thursday to strengthen the leu slightly so that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates end the year at around 8,000 lei to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'This seems to be their unofficial target,' said the dealer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said money market rates are currently around 73% annually, at\par overnight, about the same as Wednesday, but may rise slightly if\par Romania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drains some liquidity from the market.\par -By Adam Brown (401) 210-8197 adam@mail.kappa.ro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0822GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtci09q0r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
