\par\par \b \uc2  ROMANIA C.BANK SOAKS UP MONEY MARKET FUNDS. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  further on the local interbank market on Thursday by mopping up money market funds to ease pressure on the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It has taken one-week leu deposits at rates near 90 percent," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  "It is now trying to take funds but the price they are offering seems to be too low," said another operator. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  Operators said the BNR's actions on the money market came on the back of a slide in short-term prices to around 60/90 percent from rates of about 100/120 percent in early trading on Wednesday. The drop, combined with increased dollar demand from importers, put the leu under pressure. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, dealers said the BNR had sold dollars to cushion a downswing of the leu. The unit responded by firming towards 7,920/970 to the dollar from quotes near 7,970/8,015 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  (( Mirela Eremia, Bucharest newsroom +40 1 312-0264)) REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtc4010ik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
