\par\par \b \uc2  ROMANIA C.BANK SELLS DOLLARS TO TEMPER LEU SLIDE. \b0\par\par\uc2 130 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market on Thursday, selling dollars to cushion a downswing of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They sold near 7,970 lei to the dollar," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in several waves," said another. \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed towards 7,920/970 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from prices near 7,970/8,015 in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the BNR was also monitoring the money market, where rates slid to around 60/90 percent, putting the leu under pressure. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. (( Mirela Eremia, Bucharest newsroom +40 1 312-0264)) REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtc4010hx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
