\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank confirms  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  on  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid undermining reserve money targets, BNR officials said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We have bought and sold dollars, seeking not only to avoid a sharper depreciation of the leu, but also to sterilise liquidity," BNR communication manager Adrian Vasilescu said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR's move was aimed at draining leu funds from the market by selling dollars rather than taking deposits from the money market," Vasilescu said. \par \par \uc2  Reserve money, also known as the monetary base or high-powered money, includes cash in circulation and in vaults and banks' minimum reserves. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BNR sold dollars to contain a fast depreciation of the leu on Wednesday after the unit's ask quotes had fallen below 8,000 to the dollar amid growing hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand. \par \par \uc2  They said the BNR sold dollars in several waves on Wednesday at prices ranging from 7,965 to 7,980, but Vasilescu declined to elaborate on prices or the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At midday, the leu recovered from its lows, helped by the BNR moves, and was trading at around 7,940/980 against opening levels of about 7,955/8,000 and nearer to its Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Vasilescu said the BNR has also tried "to prevent further upward moves in interest rates." \par \par \uc2  The BNR has repeateadly mopped up leu deposits from the market in the past month, tightening its monetary policy to combat inflation. Its moves triggered a surge in short-term rates to more than 100 percent against 50 percent in late October. ((Mirela Eremia, Bucharest newsroom +40 1 312-0264)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301il9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
