\par\par \b \uc2  Romania c.bank sells dollars to stop leu fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local interbank market selling dollars to contain a fast depreciation of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "They are selling dollars at rates ranging from 7,965 to 7,980 lei to the dollar," said a dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR stepped into the market after the leu's ask quotes had fallen below 8,000," said another trader. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  The leu opened weaker at about 7,955/8,000 to the dollar on Wednesday against Tuesday's closing quotes of around 7,940/60, as hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand picked up. Traders expected the BNR to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a sharp fall of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Leu-dollar prices hovered at about 7,980/8,010 to the dollar after the BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders said bid-ask spreads were widening. \par \par \uc2  Operators said the rise in dollar demand had been triggered by a higher import bill and some repatriations of earnings from capital markets. ((Mirela Eremia, Bucharest newsroom +40 1 312-0264)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301ijk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
