\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Stable But Seen Weakening On Repatriation \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1997\par 09:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (AP-Dow Jones)--Romania's leu traded stable on the interbank market Wednesday but traders predicted some depreciation as foreigners withdraw money from the Treasury-bill market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at between 7,710 lei and 7,730 lei on the interbank market Wednesday at 09:30 (0630 GMT), the same as Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  One trader with a foreign bank in Bucharest cited rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cancel a T-bill auction scheduled for next week, encouraging further repatriation after the cancellation of Tuesday's weekly auction. \par \par \uc2  The government has canceled three of the last four auctions and traders said several foreigners are buying dollars to take out of the country. \par \par \uc2  Another trader predicted the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week and instead will allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate to as much as 7,800 lei to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'If the foreigners have to pay more lei for the dollar, this will discourage repatriation,' said the trader. 'They'll probably support the leu again when the T-bill auctions are held normally.' \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He predicted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't buy or sell dollars this week but\par may borrow some lei from the market if depreciation proves too rapid.\par -By Adam Brown (401)-210-8197 adam@mail.kappa.ro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-10-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0709GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1869 