\par\par \b \uc2  ROMANIA CEN.BANK SAYS MONITORING TRADE BALANCE. \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Oct 6 (Reuter) - Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu said on Monday the bank was closely watching trade balance figures to guard against movements in the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  affecting the country's competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "We are not terribly worried. But revisions of trade figures have prompted new discussions on external (balance of payments) adjustments," Isarescu told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "An appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in real terms in April and May affected the competitiveness of exports." \par \par \uc2  Isarescu said the leu's short-term moves would be monitored. Monetary and interest rate moves as well as market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be used to keep leu investments attractive. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade deficit widened to $187.4 million in July from $174.2 million in June, as imports grew more quickly than exports. The January-July deficit was $856.2 million. \par \par \uc2  The leu plunged to nearly 9,000 to the dollar in March but recovered smartly to levels around 7,000 throughout the summer. It has slipped in recent weeks to 7,700, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent sharp declines. \par \par \uc2  Iscarescu said that in the long run the BNR was considering a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor to make the exchange rate more predictable. \par \par \uc2  "We are considering an increase in transparency and predictibility," Isarescu said. \par \par \uc2  He said any corridor or trading band would differ from a classic crawling-peg system. He suggested the model of the "diagonal band" used in Israel, under which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in accordance with inflation and the balance of payments. \par \par \uc2  "We need a market-determined exchange rate," he said. "Until annual inflation is cut well below 20 percent, I favour flexibility of the exchange rate though I realise the need of more predictibility." \par \par \uc2  -- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest newsroom, +401 312-0264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dta700jw4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
