\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus: Romania Leu Seen Facing Winter Test \b0\par\par\uc2  By Adam Brown \par \uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1997\par 16:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (AP-Dow Jones)--Winter purchases of oil, although lower than in 1996, may cause Romania's leu to depreciate more quickly over the coming months, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The leu's weakness may be compounded by the removal of regulations limiting individuals from purchasing more than $500 in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although these pressures may be balanced by a long-expected - but yet to materialize - inflow of foreign investment to the country's securities markets. \par \par \uc2  The first hint of greater volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets came last week, when the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was liberalized in March of this year, the National Bank has allowed the leu to depreciate in line with inflation, while boosting its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by buying dollars on an almost daily basis. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts doubt the National Bank will be prepared to use its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to support the leu if it does begin to fall more quickly. \par \par \uc2  Parvoleta Shtereva, an analyst with ING Barings in London, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted rapidly to halt the leu's slide last week, but doubted whether it will do the same in the near future. \par \par \uc2  'I still don't believe they'll be prepared to do this on a daily basis,' said Shtereva. 'They certainly don't want to bleed reserves all through the fourth quarter.' \par \par \uc2  Shtereva said that with reserves at about $2.5 billion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the means, if not the will, to stabilize the leu. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1436GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9t07ezm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
