\par\par \b \uc2  Romania C.Bank sells dollars to prop leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 109 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, July 25 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local interbank market on Friday, selling dollars to contain growing pressure on the leu after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped about 2.5 percent on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market now. It sold me some dollars," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates ranged from 7,300 to 7,350 lei to the dollar. The leu firmed slightly to 7,200/400 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against large spreads of 7,400/600 in early trading. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7p01xcf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
