\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Leu Opens Steady -2: NBR  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1997\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  He said the amount of lei loans auctioned may drop again below the 300 billion lei level offered last week but predicted it will have little effect. \par \par \uc2  'The market is quite liquid right now so it doesn't really matter if it's only a small amount less,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The refinancing rates set in last Thursday's auction were down from 220% in the previous week but the amount of lei auctioned also dropped to 300 billion lei from 500 billion lei. \par \par \uc2  In order to avoid the high refinancing rates, banks have increased interest rates paid to clients for term deposits in leo as much as 150% yearly on one-month deposits currently. \par \par \uc2  The interest rates are up from about 80% to 90% yearly on one-month deposits about two months ago. \par \par \uc2  As a result, Romanians are depositing large amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in banks and reducing the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, say traders. \par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't reduce refinancing rates this week, predicts a trader with a foreign bank in Romania, the leu could start to rise as demand for dollars is currently low to to drops in imports. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, he predicted the NBR would then \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in the\par market, buying dollars.\par     --Adam Brown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-04-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0658GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt41029of\par }\page